From f23ebf2d9d4bff000499b208a2c5b8474c87c126 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Catania <jaca101@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:44:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Reapply the Scribus stylesheet after a palette change,
 once ADS is done

When the system switches between light and dark mode, Qt emits
QStyleHints::colorSchemeChanged before it updates the application palette
(QGuiApplicationPrivate::handleThemeChanged). The existing workaround
reapplied the Scribus stylesheet from that signal, i.e. with the old
palette. ApplicationPaletteChange then reaches the main window as a
posted event, and the ADS dock manager's event filter on that window
reloads ADS's bundled stylesheet over the Scribus one. Result: after a
system theme switch, active dock tabs kept ADS styling (grey tabs in dark
mode) instead of the Scribus stylesheet.

The main window receives its PaletteChange right after that
ApplicationPaletteChange has gone through the ADS filter. Reapply the
Scribus stylesheet from there, queued, so it wins over ADS and is built
from the new palette. The call is skipped until initScMW() has created
the styled widgets, since the splash screen processes events earlier.

Verified on macOS 26 by switching system appearance dark -> light ->
dark: active dock tabs now match the startup styling in both modes, and
CPU stays idle (no refresh loop).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 scribus/scribus.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scribus/scribus.cpp b/scribus/scribus.cpp
index d88956947..9061e3198 100644
--- a/scribus/scribus.cpp
+++ b/scribus/scribus.cpp
@@ -1930,7 +1930,15 @@ void ScribusMainWindow::changeEvent(QEvent *e)
 	if (e->type() == QEvent::LanguageChange)
 		languageChange();
 	else
+	{
+		// The main window gets its PaletteChange after the ApplicationPaletteChange that makes
+		// ADS reload its bundled stylesheet over ours, so reapply ours, with the new palette.
+		// Checked when run: the splash screen can process events before initScMW() has created
+		// the widgets setStyleSheet() styles, viewToolBar being the last of them.
+		if (e->type() == QEvent::PaletteChange)
+			QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, [this]() { if (dockManager && viewToolBar) setStyleSheet(); }, Qt::QueuedConnection);
 		QMainWindow::changeEvent(e);
+	}
 }
 
 void ScribusMainWindow::closeEvent(QCloseEvent *ce)
